    description: "The 10.0.0 release (2026-11-16) needed three attempts to get from \"release-check passed\" to \"published\". Each stop was a gate that runs only late, or a local check whose warning hides the question it asks. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/release_10_11162026/STATUS.md.\n\n1. THE I/O MANIFEST GATE RUNS ONLY IN THE RELEASE WORKFLOW (.github/workflows/release.yml, job io-manifest), which runs on a tag push or a manual dispatch. Nothing before the tag compares observed I/O with docs/io-manifest/expected.txt. So the v10.0.0 tag was signed and pushed, the run failed on four lines the release itself had added (two git queries from the \"ignored and untracked files are not analysed\" change, two renames from the write-then-rename change), nothing was published, and the tag had to be deleted and recreated (run 43947548924 failed; run 43954417304 published). The changes that added the I/O had merged days earlier (fd4fb93223, a473cd2bba).\n   WHAT IS ASKED: the comparison runs before a tag exists. Options seen: (a) scripts/release-check runs `scripts/io-manifest run` when strace is installed (the README's local recipe works on this machine: a plain venv of the built packages, the six corpus repositories at their pins under ~/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos, about 3 minutes; it reproduced the runner's four lines exactly and passed after the fix); (b) prepare-release's handoff tells the human to dispatch the Release workflow with dry_run=true on main before running tag-release (that is what verified the fix: run 43953809248); (c) a scheduled run of the io-manifest job. (a) and (b) are not exclusive.\n   ALSO: a run that reuses an output directory performs `chmod <out>/...` (the renamed file keeps the existing target's mode). The corpus starts from an empty directory and never exercises it, so that line is in no manifest.\n\n2. release-check'S DEPENDENCY AUDIT DEPENDS ON HOW STALE THE LOCAL ENVIRONMENT IS. The first prepare-release run failed on 71 advisories in seven packages that satisfied the script's old minimum versions; PR #2206 raised the minimums. This repeats at every release (9.0.0 needed the same: e67891020a). The audit question \"does a fresh install of what we ship have a known vulnerability\" is answered by a fresh environment (as CI's audit job does), not by this box's history. Re-check cadence item: WI-totak.\n\n3. release-check'S WHEEL INSTALLATION CHECK ALWAYS WARNS. Six lines \"installation check failed (may be pip version issue)\" appear for the language packages and the meta-package in every run, because `pip install <wheel> --dry-run` cannot resolve `hypergumbo-core==<new version>` before it is published. The release workflow's own \"Verify wheels\" step passes `--find-links dist/` and resolves them. A check that warns on every run cannot report a real installation failure.\n\nFixed already, listed so nobody re-files it: the release workflow's \"Secret scanning\" step never ran (`pip install trufflehog` installs a different program; `|| true` hid the usage error). PR #2209 replaced it with the pinned gitleaks and added tests/test_release_workflow_gates.py, which fails if any command in the two gate jobs is followed by `|| true`."  # 68f0
